    "total_non_empty_paragraphs": 58,
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "paragraph_index": 0,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "PRACTICAL-5",
        "char_count": 11
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 3,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "heading",
        "text": "AIM: To perform Steganography.",
        "char_count": 30
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 4,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "TOOL USED:",
        "char_count": 10
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 5,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steghide",
        "char_count": 8
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 6,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steghide is a free steganography program that allows users to hide secret files inside other files. Steganography is the technique of concealing information within another file so that the presence of the hidden information is not easily noticed.",
        "char_count": 246
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 7,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steghide hides secret data inside supported image and audio files. It supports carrier formats such as JPEG, BMP, WAV, and AU. The carrier file appears normal to an ordinary user, but it contains hidden information. Steghide can also compress and encrypt the embedded data using a passphrase.",
        "char_count": 292
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 8,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "The tool allows users to embed secret files into carrier files and extract them when required. It can also display information about a file that may contain hidden data. Steghide is useful for demonstrating how information can be concealed and recovered during digital forensic investigations.",
        "char_count": 293
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 11,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steps",
        "char_count": 5
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 12,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Open terminal in ubuntu.",
        "char_count": 24
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 13,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 14,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Create a folder “Steghide” in which, we will be storing our payload file and carrier file. Both payload and carrier files should be stored in the same folder.",
        "char_count": 158
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 16,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Create a text file with the secret message typed in it and save it as “secret.txt”. This will be our payload file/secret file.",
        "char_count": 126
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 17,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "For this, first open the text editor in Kali, type your secret message and save it as Secret.txt in the folder “Steghide”.",
        "char_count": 122
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 19,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "For this, first open the text editor in Kali, type your secret message and save it as secret.txt in the folder “Steghide”.",
        "char_count": 122
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 20,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot 2 & 3>",
        "char_count": 18
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 21,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Place the image file you want to use as the carrier file in the same folder.",
        "char_count": 76
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 22,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 24,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Hiding payload file inside the carrier file",
        "char_count": 43
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 25,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "The steghide command is used to perform steganography in Kali Linux.",
        "char_count": 68
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 26,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "To hide a payload file inside a carrier file, the embed argument and -ef option is used along with the steghide command.",
        "char_count": 120
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 27,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Syntax:",
        "char_count": 7
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 28,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "steghide embed -ef <full path of payload file> -cf <full path of carrier file> *[ef – embed file, cf – carrier file]",
        "char_count": 116
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 29,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steps",
        "char_count": 5
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 30,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Open terminal.",
        "char_count": 14
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 31,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Type ‘steghide’ and hit Enter key to see all arguments and options to be used with the steghide command.",
        "char_count": 104
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 32,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 34,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Now type the command to embed the payload file in the carrier file and hit Enter key.",
        "char_count": 85
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 35,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "steghide embed -ef <location_of_steghide/secret.txt> -cf <location_of_steghide/img.jpg>",
        "char_count": 87
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 36,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 38,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "You will be asked to enter a passphrase. Type the passphrase, re-enter it to confirm and hit Enter key.",
        "char_count": 103
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 39,
        "style": "List Paragraph",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 40,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Now the secret message is embedded in the image.",
        "char_count": 48
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 41,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Extracting secret data from a file",
        "char_count": 34
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 42,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "To extract a payload file from a carrier file, the extract argument and -sf option is used along with the steghide command.",
        "char_count": 123
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 43,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Syntax :",
        "char_count": 8
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 44,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "steghide extract -sf <full path of carrier file>",
        "char_count": 48
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 45,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "*[sf – stego file] Steps",
        "char_count": 24
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 46,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Type the command to extract payload file from carrier file in the terminal and hit Enter key.",
        "char_count": 93
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 47,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "steghide extract -sf <Location_of_steghide/img.jpg>",
        "char_count": 51
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 48,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 50,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "You will be asked to enter the passphrase. Type the passphrase and hit Enter key.",
        "char_count": 81
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 51,
        "style": "List Paragraph",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 52,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "wrote extracted data to \"screte.txt\"",
        "char_count": 36
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 53,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "To wrote the extracted date to a specified file. Type the command to extract payload from the carrier file and specified the name and location of the file.",
        "char_count": 155
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 54,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "*[-xf <filename>]      -  write the extracted data to <filename>",
        "char_count": 64
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 55,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "steghide extract -sf <Location_of_steghide/img.jpg> -xf  <Location_of_steghide/filename>",
        "char_count": 88
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 56,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Checking whether a file contains embedded secret data",
        "char_count": 53
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 57,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "To check whether a file contains embedded secret data, the info argument is used along with the steghide command.",
        "char_count": 113
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 58,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Syntax :",
        "char_count": 8
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 59,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "steghide info <filename>",
        "char_count": 24
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 61,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steps",
        "char_count": 5
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 62,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Type the command in the terminal and hit Enter key.",
        "char_count": 51
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 63,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steghide info <location_of_the_steghide/img.jpg>",
        "char_count": 48
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 64,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 66,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "You will be asked to enter the passphrase. Type the passphrase and hit Enter key.",
        "char_count": 81
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 67,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "<screenshot>",
        "char_count": 12
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 69,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "output_heading",
        "text": "OUTPUT",
        "char_count": 6
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 70,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Successfully performed steganography using Steghide.",
        "char_count": 52
      }
